SRC/xrand -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  xcrypt.c  Two things kept it from working on OS-9, both at the top of            main().  It opened its output with open(name, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT,            0600), and OS-9's open() cannot create a file, so unless the            output already existed it printed its syntax line and exited 1.            It now uses creat(), which also empties an existing output.            And it chose the direction from argv[0] -- linked as `encrypt'            it encrypts, as anything else it decrypts -- where one OS-9            module has one name, so `xcrypt' could only decrypt.  An            optional first argument -e or -d now names the direction;            without one argv[0] decides, as before.  Rebuilt -qm,            2026-09-26.  The original is xcrypt.c.ori.